  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.header": "Experimental Reactor: Build",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_1": "Build the 5×5×5 casing frame; every edge must use reactor casing.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_2": "Arrange fuel and control-rod columns freely; unused columns may stay empty.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_3": "Stack three fuel rods vertically in each column and cap it with a refueling port.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_4": "Leave control-rod columns hollow and cap them with drives; each affects cardinal neighbors only.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_5": "Place one instrument port, one or more cold inlets and one or more hot outlets on non-edge sides.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_6": "Multiple cold and hot ports are allowed; place them on valid side blocks to suit the pipe layout.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_7": "Seal every outside wall. Windows may replace casing on non-edge side blocks.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_8": "Check the instrument port with a Create Wrench. Load fuel only after the structure forms.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.header": "Experimental Reactor: Fuel and Control Rods",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_1": "Fuel and control columns can be placed in different positions and numbers; layout sets heat and control coverage.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_2": "Loaded fuel columns strengthen one another across cardinal neighbors; diagonal neighbors do not interact.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_3": "Overclocking raises heat and fuel use; more neighboring fuel columns strengthen the feedback.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_4": "Control rods limit only cardinally adjacent fuel columns; deeper insertion means lower power.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_5": "With multiple neighboring rods, their insertion depths are averaged; one fully inserted rod is not enough to stop the column.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_6": "Insert all neighboring control rods to stop that fuel column; redstone shutdown works through rod insertion.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_7": "A loaded column with no neighboring control rod runs at full power, even during SCRAM.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_rods.text_8": "Rods and redstone cannot stop these columns or remove fuel while it produces heat; wait for exhaustion.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.header": "Experimental Reactor: Run and Stop",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_1": "Before starting, connect the coolant loop and confirm the fuel is loaded.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_2": "Raise the rods gradually to start fission. Deeper insertion means lower power.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_3": "Cold coolant absorbs heat and leaves through the hot port. Keep both directions open.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_4": "Engineer Goggles show heat production, cooling rate, and coolant stock at the instrument port.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_5": "Fully insert the control rods to stop. A redstone signal at the instrument port inserts every movable rod.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_6": "Fission stops before residual heat does. Keep coolant circulating until the core cools.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_operation.text_7": "When the signal is removed, the control rod returns to its previous target depth.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.header": "Experimental Reactor: Load and Replace Fuel",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_1": "Each refueling port serves the fuel column directly below it and holds one assembly.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_2": "With a formed reactor and a non-fissioning column, right-click the port with a fresh enriched uranium fuel assembly.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_3": "After the fuel is exhausted, it becomes a depleted uranium fuel assembly.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_4": "Insert the neighboring control rod and wait for fission to stop in the target column. Keep cooling residual heat.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_5": "Take the old assembly with an empty hand, then load a fresh one.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor_refueling.text_6": "Power a Create Mechanical Arm to take fresh fuel from supply and deliver spent fuel to receiving storage. Hoppers cannot access the fuel port.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.header": "Uranium Slurry Enrichment Centrifuge",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_1": "The centrifuge separates uranium slurry into low-enriched uranium dust, depleted uranium dust, and recoverable water.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_2": "The machine is two blocks tall. Leave room above for the inlet pipe.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_3": "Power the centrifuge from below. Processing starts once the speed is stable.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_4": "Uranium slurry can only enter from the top.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_5": "Each 1000 mB of uranium slurry yields 1 low-enriched uranium dust, 7 depleted uranium dust, and 1000 mB of water. Higher speeds process it faster.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_6": "Both halves can output powder or water from any of their four sides. Use brass funnels to collect the powders separately and pipes to recover water.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_7": "Processing pauses if power is lost, speed is unstable, or outputs are blocked. Progress is preserved.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.enrichment_centrifuge.text_8": "When the bearing wears out, stop the power. Hold one heavy bearing and right-click the front of the lower section to repair it.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.header": "High-pressure boiler: Build and zones",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_1": "By default, length, width, and height are each 5–11 blocks and can be adjusted separately. This example is 7×7×7.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_2": "Place the built-in heat exchangers on the base. Hot inlets share this layer and may replace non-corner bottom-edge casing.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_3": "Complete the partition with reheating sections and casing. Cold outlets share its layer and stay off the edges.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_4": "Leave at least one layer above and below the partition. Place water and controller ports in the water zone.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_5": "Place steam ports in the steam zone. Side ports face horizontally outward.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_6": "Place the safety valve on top and leave its outlet clear. Add water, steam, and coolant ports as needed.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_build.text_7": "Effective heat loops equal the smaller count of built-in heat exchangers and reheating sections.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.header": "High-pressure boiler: Connect and run",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_1": "By default, length, width, and height are each 5–11 blocks and can be adjusted separately.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_2": "Water-zone volume determines water capacity; steam-zone volume determines steam capacity.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_3": "Fill the water zone first. Then circulate coolant on separate lines.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_4": "Start the cold-coolant return before supplying heat. A blocked return limits further heat intake.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_5": "With water supplied and cold return flowing, start the hot-coolant input to heat the boiler.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_6": "With other conditions equal, a larger water zone warms more slowly.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_7": "Water boils before steam is reheated; a larger steam zone pressurizes more slowly.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_operation.text_8": "Use goggles to check boiler status, temperature, pressure, and effective heat loops.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.header": "High-pressure boiler: Steam output and pressure",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.text_1": "New steam is classified by actual temperature and pressure. Ordinary and supercritical steam use separate inventories.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.text_2": "Both inventories share zone capacity and boiler pressure. Changing the minimum does not change stored steam types.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.text_3": "Choose a steam type at each outlet with Create's native option. Each drains only its selected inventory; no downgrade conversion occurs.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.text_4": "The minimum output pressure ranges from 0–100. Lower it to 10%. It gates normal output; it is not a target boiler pressure or safety-valve pressure.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.high_pressure_boiler_steam.text_5": "Stored, heat-qualified supercritical steam can drain to the shared minimum below the new-steam classification pressure. Its type stays unchanged; keep steam types on separate lines.",
